  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile RNA (scvi_n200) is the strongest configuration found so far (acc ~0.65), while image-only models are very weak (acc ~0.21-0.23). The only multimodal test (config_034, singleprofile) showed only a marginal gain over RNA-only (0.532 vs 0.520), suggesting image adds little in singleprofile mode. Critical uncertainty: does the multiprofile setting—which unlocked a ~13% gain for RNA alone—also unlock complementary signal from the image modality? This experiment (config_038: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) directly tests whether the best RNA encoder combined with the best image encoder in a multiprofile multimodal setting can exceed the 0.653 RNA-only ceiling. It uses transformer aggregation (marginally better than avgpool in config_006) and concat fusion (the only fusion tested in config_034). If it beats 0.653, image is a useful complement in the richer profile space; if it does not, we can confidently deprioritize all remaining multimodal and image-only configurations, saving budget for RNA-encoder exploration (e.g., scgpt)."
}

